## 4. Q&A additions from the new evidence

- **"If ESG was financially valuable, why did NWD still hit trouble?"** The sustainability-linked and green instruments cover only a fraction of debt. The crisis came from 11 SKIES, property impairments and leverage, none of which ESG ratings address.
- **"Wasn't the 11 SKIES green loan a failure of your triage?"** Yes, and that is why the profitability test goes on top of the certification test.
- **"Why keep K11 if its assets are now collateral?"** It is the part lenders and the C-REIT market will pay for. The risk is concentration, so we stay capital-light.
- **"Isn't your plan too ESG-friendly given the backlash?"** The lecture shows the backlash (L5), but Mainland policy still supports ESG (L9–13) and NWD's Mainland assets such as K11 ELYSEA (LEED Platinum, 3-Star) depend on it.

